{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>Ahazat</b> — Rabbi Moses said: it is an adjective [describing] the name [noun], like <i>atzumot</i>, for the eyelids guard the eyes by closing, and the meaning is: they seized [me] before my eyes closed and I did not sleep." "<b>Nepa'amti</b> — like <i>vetipa'em rucho</i>. I was struck so deeply that I could not speak."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 77, :notes {0 "Resolved epithet 'Rabbi Moses' as Ibn Ezra's contemporary Moses ibn Tiktok or similar; left untranslated as proper name."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:34:45.712460435Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}